{
  "category": "Light Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "The light it emits is so bright that it can illuminate the sea's surface from a depth of over three miles.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "It blinds prey with an intense burst of light, then swallows the immobilized prey in a single gulp.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "This POKéMON uses the bright part of its body, which changed from a dorsal fin, to lure prey.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "LANTURN is nicknamed “the deep-sea star” for its illuminated antenna. This POKéMON produces light by causing a chemical reaction between bacteria and its bodily fluids inside the antenna.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "LANTURN is known to emit light. If you peer down into the dark sea from a ship at night, you can sometimes see this POKéMON’s light rising from the depths where it swims. It gives the sea an appearance of a starlit night.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "The light-emitting orbs on its back are very bright. They are formed from a part of its dorsal fin. This POKéMON illuminates the inky darkness of deep seas.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "It blinds prey with an intense burst of light, then swallows the immobilized prey in a single gulp.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "The light it emits is so bright that it can illuminate the sea’s surface from a depth of over three miles.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "LANTURN’s light can shine up from great depths. It is nicknamed “The Deep-Sea Star.”",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "LANTURN’s light can shine up from great depths. It is nicknamed “The Deep-Sea Star.”",
