    {
      "text": "Lanturn is nicknamed “the deep-sea star” for its illuminated antenna. This Pokémon produces light by causing a chemical reaction between bacteria and its bodily fluids inside the antenna.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lanturn is known to emit light. If you peer down into the dark sea from a ship at night, you can sometimes see this Pokémon’s light rising from the depths where it swims. It gives the sea an appearance of a starlit night.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "Should you peer into the ocean at night and see a light shining like the stars, that is Lanturn.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon flashes a bright light that blinds its prey. This creates an opening for it to deliver an electrical attack.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "When the bacteria living inside its antennae absorb Lanturn’s bodily fluids, a strong luminescent effect is produced.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It lives far down in the depths of the ocean. It blinds its prey with light, using the moment they’re dazzled to swallow them whole.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "The light it emits is so bright that it can illuminate the sea’s surface from a depth of over three miles.",
